item><title><![CDATA[Rank-based merit list to replace percentile for NEET PG: Panel to SC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rank-based-merit-list-to-replace-percentile-for-neet-pg-panel-to-sc/articleshow/135516685.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135516685.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The National Medical Commission has officially approved a shift from a percentile to a rank-based system for NEET admissions, which aims to improve the current postgraduate medical course admission process. This change comes amid concerns over the possible decrease in qualifying scores for NEET-PG 2025. The commission is focused on preserving the integrity of medical examinations and has also suggested equitable salary structures for medical residents.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rank-based-merit-list-to-replace-percentile-for-neet-pg-panel-to-sc/articleshow/135516685.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rank-based-merit-list-to-replace-percentile-for-neet-pg-panel-to-sc/articleshow/135516685.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T05:37:04+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135516735,imgsize-67588.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian tourist killed, PIO injured as copters collide during Everest rescue]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indian-tourist-killed-pio-injured-as-copters-collide-during-everest-rescue/articleshow/135516590.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135516590.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indian-tourist-killed-pio-injured-as-copters-collide-during-everest-rescue/articleshow/135516590.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indian-tourist-killed-pio-injured-as-copters-collide-during-everest-rescue/articleshow/135516590.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T05:27:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vishant V Agarwala</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135516637,imgsize-121800.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Take on Modi in Parliament, FM Sitharaman tells Rahul Gandhi on debate challenge]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/take-on-modi-in-parliament-fm-sitharaman-tells-rahul-gandhi-on-debate-challenge/articleshow/135516272.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135516272.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/take-on-modi-in-parliament-fm-sitharaman-tells-rahul-gandhi-on-debate-challenge/articleshow/135516272.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/take-on-modi-in-parliament-fm-sitharaman-tells-rahul-gandhi-on-debate-challenge/articleshow/135516272.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T05:11:22+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135516303,imgsize-134450.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Still waiting for a debate: Rahul Gandhi to PM Modi]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/still-waiting-for-a-debate-rahul-gandhi-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135516252.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135516252.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/still-waiting-for-a-debate-rahul-gandhi-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135516252.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/still-waiting-for-a-debate-rahul-gandhi-to-pm-modi/articleshow/135516252.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T05:00:29+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135516262,imgsize-67032.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[BJP, allies slam Neha Bora for 'anti-Hindu' remarks]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-allies-slam-neha-bora-for-anti-hindu-remarks/articleshow/135515118.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135515118.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Neha Bora of AISA has come under fire for her remarks about the Brahmanical system and temple safety. Her comments have been interpreted as reinforcing claims of anti-Hindu sentiments within Rahul Gandhi's ecosystem. BJP spokesperson Gaurav Bhatia condemned her statements, accusing her of insulting priests and promoting divisive rhetoric. LJP chief Chirag Paswan urged Congress to reconsider its association with her and similar figures.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-allies-slam-neha-bora-for-anti-hindu-remarks/articleshow/135515118.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-allies-slam-neha-bora-for-anti-hindu-remarks/articleshow/135515118.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T04:15:20+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135515769,imgsize-78920.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Judge needn't face strictures for typos in judgement: SC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/judge-neednt-face-strictures-for-typos-in-judgement-sc/articleshow/135513583.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135513583.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant move, the Supreme Court intervened to address remarks made by the Rajasthan high court about a trial judge. This action stemmed from minor errors in a ruling, which the High Court harshly criticized, despite the fact that these did not alter the outcome of the case.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/judge-neednt-face-strictures-for-typos-in-judgement-sc/articleshow/135513583.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/judge-neednt-face-strictures-for-typos-in-judgement-sc/articleshow/135513583.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T03:46:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Amit Anand Choudhary</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135513661,imgsize-126618.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Encouraged by response to defence of SIR, BJP plans next political push]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/encouraged-by-response-to-defence-of-sir-bjp-plans-next-political-push/articleshow/135513330.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135513330.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The BJP is concluding its initial campaign phase to promote the SIR initiative. Union home minister Amit Shah has reached out to Congress, proposing a parliamentary discussion on the topic. Their strategy focuses on addressing the opposition's criticism related to the SIR and electoral setbacks. A BJP-commissioned survey reveals substantial public backing for the initiative, with the next campaign phase due to launch after Diwali celebrations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/encouraged-by-response-to-defence-of-sir-bjp-plans-next-political-push/articleshow/135513330.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/encouraged-by-response-to-defence-of-sir-bjp-plans-next-political-push/articleshow/135513330.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T03:00:13+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135513353,imgsize-60840.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[SC to define right to privacy of protesters in public places]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-to-define-right-to-privacy-of-protesters-in-public-places/articleshow/135513072.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135513072.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-to-define-right-to-privacy-of-protesters-in-public-places/articleshow/135513072.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sc-to-define-right-to-privacy-of-protesters-in-public-places/articleshow/135513072.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-04T02:34:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dhananjay Mahapatra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135513141,imgsize-59328.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Right to protest can't justify endless occupation of a site: SC]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/right-to-protest-cant-justify-endless-occupation-of-a-site-sc/articleshow/135512694.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135512694.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/right-to-protest-cant-justify-endless-occupation-of-a-site-sc/articleshow/135512694.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/right-to-protest-cant-justify-endless-occupation-of-a-site-sc/articleshow/135512694.cms]]></