y-tests-expandable-space-habitat-tech-in-near-space-mission/articleshow/135509381.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T23:27:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chethan Kumar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135509498,imgsize-121120.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Deeply touched': PM Modi thanks Bhutan King for dedicating sacred stupa in his honour]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/deeply-touched-pm-modi-thanks-bhutan-king-for-dedicating-sacred-stupa-in-his-honour/articleshow/135509436.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135509436.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Prime Minister Narendra Modi has expressed heartfelt thanks for the dedication of a sacred stupa by Bhutan's King Jigme Khesar Namgyel Wangchuck. Unveiled on November 1, this stupa strengthens the enduring friendship and cultural ties between India and Bhutan. This initiative highlights Bhutan's commitment to boosting its Buddhist identity and serves as a token of gratitude for India's continuous support in its developmental journey.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/deeply-touched-pm-modi-thanks-bhutan-king-for-dedicating-sacred-stupa-in-his-honour/articleshow/135509436.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/deeply-touched-pm-modi-thanks-bhutan-king-for-dedicating-sacred-stupa-in-his-honour/articleshow/135509436.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T23:25:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135509473,imgsize-99320.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[One move, two gains: NHAI to desilt Bihar rivers and build roads with excavated material]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-desilt-bihar-rivers-and-build-roads-with-excavated-material/articleshow/135509375.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135509375.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Bihar's government has signed an agreement with the road transport ministry for river desilting to reduce flooding. The excavated silt and sand will be utilized in highway construction projects across the state. This initiative aims to improve water flow in rivers while providing construction materials at no cost. Bihar Chief Minister Samrat Choudhary emphasized the impact of flooding on the state's agriculture and infrastructure.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-desilt-bihar-rivers-and-build-roads-with-excavated-material/articleshow/135509375.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/one-move-two-gains-nhai-to-desilt-bihar-rivers-and-build-roads-with-excavated-material/articleshow/135509375.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-03T23:21:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dipak K Dash</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135509360,imgsize-132106.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[1.5-tonne Nasa space observatory set to crash on Earth today, possibility of debris parts falling in India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-5-tonne-nasa-space-observatory-set-to-crash-on-earth-today-possibility-of-debris-parts-falling-in-india/articleshow/135509019.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135509019.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/1-5-tonne-nasa-space-observatory-set-to-crash-on-earth-